     "intro": [
      "QF continues to advance research and policy initiatives to drive positive change for Qatar and other hot and arid climates. Earthna’s policy reports provide actionable insights and regionally grounded strategies that inform decision-makers, foster collaboration, and accelerate sustainability priorities nationally and across the Gulf and MENA regions. Earthna is working primarily to advance knowledge and action across sustainability frameworks, circular economies, energy transition, climate change, biodiversity and ecosystems, cities and the built environment, and education, ethics, and faith. Since 2023, Earthna and other key stakeholders have supported the publication of annual white papers alongside the QNDCC. These documents distill the dialogue’s key themes and offer concrete policy recommendations, reinforcing Qatar’s role in translating climate discourse into action."
     ],
     "items": [
      "The Earthna Center for a Sustainable Future collaborates with and supports the Ministry of Environment and Climate Change to ensure its research aligns with long-term government priorities. Earthna is a vital partner of the <strong>Qatar National Dialogue on Climate Change</strong> (QNDCC), an event to address climate change and promote sustainable development in Qatar. The 2025 edition of the QNDCC, co-hosted by Earthna and the Abdullah Bin Hamad Al-Attiyah Foundation, reinforced Qatar’s leadership in regional climate policy. Held in collaboration with MoECC and supported by the GCC Secretariat General, the two-day event focused on strengthening cross-border cooperation among GCC countries and leveraging shared expertise to address climate challenges. Elevated by global and national partnerships, including the UNFCCC Climate High-Level Champions and the Race to Resilience, QNDCC 2025 was recognized by the (Conference of the Parties) COP30 Presidency as a flagship Action Agenda event on the road to Belém, further cementing Qatar’s leadership in regional and international climate policy.",
      "QF’s most prominent sustainability-focused advocacy platform is the <strong>biannual Earthna Summit</strong>, which brings together national and global experts to share insights and translate academic insights into policy and practice, explore areas of convergence, and share best practices. The inaugural edition was held in 2023 under the theme of \"Building New Sustainability Pathways for Hot and Arid Environments.\" The second edition of the Earthna Summit under the theme of \"Building our Legacy: Sustainability, Innovation and Traditional Knowledge\" in April 2025 with over 2000 experts underscored Qatar’s commitment to advancing sustainability in hot and arid environments, by drawing on its rich cultural heritage and unique ecosystems. It saw the launch of the <strong>Arid Cities Network</strong>, a pioneering city-level partnership and community of practice designed to accelerate sustainable and resilient solutions for hot and arid regions. Earthna has issued several papers on essential areas such as sustainable tourism and the circular economy, urban climate change governance and the need to build city networks, sustainability frameworks for arid environments, and more. This research combines data-driven initiatives to develop policy recommendations based on initiatives tested in Education City.",
      "To honor and promote the critical role of the traditional knowledge passed down through generations in addressing the pressing environmental issues of our time, Earthna launched the <strong>Earthna Prize</strong> in 2024. The Earthna Prize recognizes communities and organizations globally whose work aligns with one or more of the prize’s themes: water resource management, food security, sustainable urbanism, and land stewardship. Four Earthna Prize winners, who share a US $1 million prize pool, were announced at the Earthna Summit in April 2025. They were selected from 12 finalists who were shortlisted from 400 applications from more than 100 countries. The winners may use the award to support their work’s development, continuation, and scaling. By showcasing outstanding efforts, the Prize aims to aims to inspire a wider community to champion environmental stewardship and contribute to a more resilient and environmentally conscious world. The second cycle of the Earthna Prize is elevating environmentally focused solutions rooted in traditional knowledge, recognizing and scaling initiatives addressing critical ecosystems through a $1 million award provided at the Earthna Summit 2027.",
      "QF further contributed to planning and policy development for Qatar’s long-term sustainability. At the United Nations Industrial Development Organization (UNIDO) General Conference and Global Industry Summit, Earthna signed a Joint Declaration with UNIDO and launched a joint publication \"Industrial Policies for Diversification in Qatar\" in February 2026. The publication outlines key recommendations to leverage advanced technologies, renewable energy and circular economy practices to shape transformative industrial policies.",
      "Stakeholders from government, academia and industry came together to discuss Qatar’s long-term preparedness and sustainability at HBKU-QEERI’s Qatar Resilience Symposium. The symposium touched on topics like emergency preparedness, risk management, and how to integrate resilience into national planning frameworks. Through research initiatives like the Proactive Resilience Plan (PReP) and Resilient Solutions for Vulnerabilities and Emergencies (ReSolVE), Qatar is advancing its capacity to build a more resilient future.",
      "Over the past decade, QF has organized the Qatar Sustainability Week (QSW) in collaboration with the Ministry of Environment and Climate Change (MECC), an annual national platform that brings together governmental leaders, educators, students, professionals, and civil society to accelerate the country’s transition to a more sustainable future. Through hundreds of activations like competitions and exhibitions around Doha, QSW fosters sustainability literacy and encourages long-term behavioral change by making sustainable actions and practices more accessible. In its 10<sup>th</sup> edition in 2025, QSW held over 700 events, including hundreds of visitors to Green Island, an 8,000-square-meter zone located in Education City that serves as Qatar’s first community-focused recycling hub.",
      "The <strong>first sustainability report for QF</strong> has also been completed. <em>Building a Sustainable Qatar: A Report on Qatar Foundation’s Leadership and Progress</em> provides a comprehensive overview of QF’s sustainability journey from 2009 to 2025, highlighting achievements across operations, research, policy, and community engagement. Reflecting QF’s commitment to translating knowledge into impact, the report features the Sustainability Thematic Executive Committee’s 10-year targets, showcases ecosystem-wide research and testbed initiatives, and explores how traditional knowledge can inform sustainable solutions for the future. It also includes a map of QF’s sustainability assets across Education City, illustrating how sustainability is embedded throughout the ecosystem and contributes to building a more sustainable Qatar."
     ],
