     "intro": [],
     "items": [
      "<strong>Doha Debates</strong> continues to expand its global impact by mentoring students through its Ambassador Program and providing extended opportunities for youth to actively shape its programming. The program now includes 160+ ambassadors from over 40 countries, forming a growing network of young leaders committed to intercultural dialogue, civic engagement, and positive change in their communities and beyond. Since its relaunch in 2018, Doha Debates has engaged young people from more than 230 countries and territories, building a community of truth-seeking, civic-minded participants who use majlis-style debate to explore differences constructively.",
      "Its ecosystem includes weekly podcast episodes and the Doha Debates Podcast, often featuring Ambassador Program alumni in in-depth conversations that bring together diverse perspectives to find common ground. Its Negotiators series also achieved international recognition, with the episode \"The Afghan Impasse\" winning the 17th Shorty Award for News & Politics Podcast.",
      "Through its global programming, Doha Debates highlights voices from both the Global South and Global North on issues that shape shared futures. In collaboration with Qatar’s Years of Culture, it has expanded its town hall series internationally, including a Latin America edition in Argentina in December 2025 on \"How should we reinvent the city?\" and a UK session at the Bradford Literature Festival on \"National identity and the modern state.\"",
      "Doha Debates is also strengthening its digital and immersive engagement through partnerships with Shared Studios via the Doha Portal, enabling real-time, majlis-style dialogue across geographies. In its new collaboration with Al Jazeera Media Network, hosts engage students from Education City and beyond in structured debates that challenge assumptions and deepen critical discussion on global issues. Looking ahead, Doha Debates will further scale its global town halls, expand the Ambassador Program, continue its weekly podcast episodes, and produce a new season of its flagship show, strengthening its role as a platform reshaping global discourse through dialogue, inclusion, and youth leadership.",
      "QF fosters free thought, open discussions, and constructive debate with a specific focus on doing so in Arabic. <strong>QatarDebate</strong> is Qatar’s National Debating Organization for Qatar and is a prize-winning debate program that has hosted thought-provoking discussions and engaged young minds from over 75 countries on global and local issues. Active for more than 16 years, QatarDebate is a civic engagement initiative that develops and supports the standard of open discussion and debate among students and youth in Qatar and the broader Arab world. To date, its programs have engaged more than 28,800 students from over 3,300 schools and universities, strengthening debate skills in both Arabic and English among youth and young adults.",
      "In January 2026, QatarDebate Center hosted its third edition of the <strong>Mutual Dialogue Summit.</strong> In strategic partnership with the Ministry of Sports and Youth, and with Msheireb Museums as cultural partner, it provided an outcome‑driven platform for youth to engage in substantive dialogue on key local and regional issues. It brought more than 100 young participants together with experts and decision‑makers to exchange perspectives and co‑develop practical responses to emerging challenges. The Summit demonstrated the role of informed dialogue in strengthening youth civic participation and solution‑oriented thinking."
     ],
