     "title": "Championing Women and Girls in Sport",
     "group": "Social Responsibility",
     "align": [
      "cohesion",
      "life"
     ],
     "intro": [],
     "items": [
      "QF and QNB Group signed a five-year agreement to rename Education City Stadium as <strong>QNB Education City Stadium</strong> in June 2026, reinforcing the venue’s post-World Cup legacy as a hub for sport, community engagement, and opportunities for women and girls. The partnership reflects the shared commitment of two national institutions to advancing sport as a driver of social development, inclusion, youth empowerment, and healthy lifestyles. Building on the stadium’s role as a setting tailored to support women’s and girls’ participation in sport, the agreement supports QF’s ambition to position the venue as a place of sporting excellence, inclusivity, and inspiration.",
      "In line with national priorities, QF is making strides in <strong>supporting girls’ and women’s-only sports teams in Qatar</strong>, such as Her Time to Play, which provides opportunities for women and girls to play basketball and pursue careers in coaching and athletic leadership. Additionally, QF hosted the Junior Premier League GCC Warriors Cup Qatar, the largest girls’ football competition in the Gulf Region.",
      "The forthcoming <strong>MAS Foundation</strong> (currently in development) will champion sports for women and girls in Qatar and beyond. It will establish a national sports academy for women, conduct sport for development projects to create more equitable, inclusive and educated communities using sport across QF and the region, and develop pathways and pipelines for women across the sport ecosystem to build a healthier and more robust women’s sport environment in Qatar.",
      "Aiming to cultivate an inclusive, accessible sporting culture across the nation, region and beyond, QF, Education Above All Foundation and the International Olympic Committee launched the Circle In project in 2025 to nurture more equitable education communities across Asia and the Middle East and North Africa region, through sport.",
      "Offerings in Education City continue to be expanded, providing fit-for-purpose spaces where women and girls can participate in athletics regardless of their different needs or cultural considerations. QF organizes <strong>Ladies Night</strong> every week in Oxygen Park during the cooler months, and it was also introduced at Education City Stadium in 2023, offering women and girls a space to exercise and socialize when the weather gets warmer. Other facilities like Education City Golf Club, the Women’s Track and Field, the Dome Padel Club, and Al-Shaqab Equestrian Center provide ladies-only sports and programming throughout the year. In 2025, QF’s Ladies Night returned with new exciting additions, including a dedicated STEM Zone spotlighting sports, health, fitness and innovation.",
      "PUE and the Qatar Cycling and Triathlon Federation signed a MoU in 2026 to advance sports development, inclusion, and community engagement. The partnership will expand access to specialized cycling and triathlon programs for students and the wider community in Qatar, with a particular focus on girls and students with accessibility needs, while leveraging QF’s sporting facilities. It will also support coach development, workshops, and joint initiatives that strengthen participation and foster a sustainable culture of sport. By broadening access to quality sporting opportunities, the collaboration supports Qatar’s health, inclusion, and youth development priorities, helping to build resilient and engaged communities.",
      "QF’s sport-for-development approach is also exemplified in its multi-year collaboration signed in 2026 with the Basketball Africa League (BAL), a professional league established by FIBA and NBA Africa, which makes QF the BAL’s first Official Community Partner. Facilitated by Qatar Sports Investments, the partnership reflects QF’s belief in strategic partnerships that bring together complementary strengths, expand opportunity, and create sustainable impact beyond any single institution. Through this collaboration, QF supports BAL’s social impact programming and efforts to make basketball more accessible across Africa.",
      "QF’s report on \"<strong>Championing Sports for Women and Girls Progress Report 2022-2025</strong>\" explores how QF is contributing to Qatar’s health in line with national priorities through ongoing efforts in women’s and girls’ sports."
     ],
